 r"I am writing to apply for the Graduate AI Software Developer position at Reply in London, for the Summer/Autumn 2027 intake. I have completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after graduating from Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience, I have built Python pipelines and tools around large language models, from retrieval-augmented generation to AI agents, and used them to solve problems for real users. I am particularly interested in this role because it combines software development with generative AI on client projects.",

 r"What attracts me most to Reply is that the AI work is built into real client solutions rather than left as a proof of concept. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved. The posting describes integrating AI models, APIs and cloud services into enterprise applications, alongside training, hackathons and innovation labs, and that is the kind of engineering environment I want to grow in.",

 r"In my current role at TikTok Shop UK, I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build KPI frameworks and dashboards for operations, product and commercial teams. When my supervisor asked me to configure a merchant campaign by hand, I saw the logic after a few examples and built an AI agent with Claude Code, with a multi-step design and a validation step to check its accuracy. I delivered it before the deadline and it cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent. This experience taught me that an AI tool is only useful if people can trust its output.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology, I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a patient-facing AI product for a pharmaceutical client. I built a Python pipeline that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and search augmentation and scored more than 2,400 responses with an LLM-as-judge framework, co-built a medically reviewed knowledge graph of 123 entities and 161 relations, and designed blinded A/B tests of its effect on answer quality. I also built a regex and LLM extraction pipeline that turned 4,800 patient consultation threads into structured data. Defining how a system will be evaluated before building it is the habit I would bring to Reply's client projects.",

 r"My MSc gave me hands-on experience of building end to end. My dissertation used data from 458,840 UK Biobank participants and was delivered as an interactive Streamlit application, and I led a group project fine-tuning ClinicalBERT and PubMedBERT models with Hugging Face Transformers. At Ipsos Strategy3 I worked directly with client stakeholders, which is where I learned to explain a technical result in terms of what it means for the client.",

 r"I would bring Reply strong Python, practical experience with LLM APIs, retrieval and AI agents, working knowledge of Git, Docker and AWS, and experience presenting technical work to clients. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship, and I am based in London.",

